 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Finite generation over degree zero",
 "statement": "If $I=(f_0,\\ldots,f_r)$, then $\\mathcal R_A(I)$ is generated as an algebra\nover its degree-zero piece by $f_0t,\\ldots,f_rt$. In particular it is of\nfinite type over $\\mathcal R_A(I)_0$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-def-nagata-sketch-data/prop-nagata-rees-finite-generation.md",
